# House segment for the real Pi (docs/user_guide/home_network.md). Copy to
# /etc/pi-fortress/house.env and run `pf apply`. Delete the file and
# apply again to remove the segment.
#
# The USB Ethernet interface with a cable to the LAN port of the access point.
HOUSE_IF=eth1
HOUSE_NET=10.78.0.0/24
HOUSE_IP=10.78.0.1
HOUSE_DHCP_START=10.78.0.100
HOUSE_DHCP_END=10.78.0.199
# The address of the admin machine (reserve it in /etc/pi-fortress/house.hosts
# as "mac,ip,name"). Only this address may ssh to the Pi from the house
# and to the agent (AGENT_IP) on the agent segment. Keep empty for no holes.
HOUSE_ADMIN_IP=
# Makes the destination of the house->agent hole wider than the single
# AGENT_IP, for AGENT_COUNT > 1 (the admin machine must reach agent2, agent3,
# ...). An address or an a-b range, inside AGENT_NET. Empty keeps the hole
# for AGENT_IP only. No effect without HOUSE_ADMIN_IP -- only that key opens
# the hole. This key only makes the reach of the hole wider.
#HOUSE_SSH_TO=10.77.0.10-10.77.0.12
# Upstream resolver for house lookups. The default is DNS_UPSTREAM, or
# the DoT stub when DOT_IPS is set. A value here is plaintext, so apply
# refuses it while DOT_IPS is set.
#HOUSE_DNS_UPSTREAM=9.9.9.9
# The DNS-over-TLS provider of the house, when it should not share the
# provider of the agents and the Pi itself. Empty means that it shares it.
# Needs DOT_AUTH_NAME and DOT_IPS set in net.env also: this is a second
# stub next to the stub of the box. It is not a way to enable DoT for the
# house alone. Refused together with HOUSE_DNS_UPSTREAM (the house forwards
# to one resolver). With WG_IF, the stub dials it through the tunnel. A
# stopped tunnel leaves the house without DNS, never on the uplink.
#
# Quote the address list. pf render parses this file and does not source
# it. But the file has shell format, and some tools source it. Without
# quotes, the shell reads the second address as a command. The usual reason
# for a separate provider here is a Control D profile -- the id in the
# name selects the profile, so it must be your own.
#HOUSE_DOT_AUTH_NAME=abcd1234xyz.dns.controld.com
#HOUSE_DOT_IPS="76.76.2.22 76.76.10.22"
# Secure DNS: on lets house devices use your own secure-DNS endpoint
# (house_private_dns.domains, for example abcd1234xyz.dns.controld.com) over
# DoT and DoH (tcp 853/443) at its pinned addresses (house_private_dns.ips,
# single addresses). The gateway sinkholes other profiles of the provider.
# This applies to the full segment. The Pi then does not see or filter the
# DNS of that device. UDP to them (QUIC, DoQ) stays closed.
#HOUSE_PRIVATE_DNS=off
# Direct IP: on drops a new HTTP or HTTPS connection to an address that
# the house DNS did not give (an app or device that goes around the sinkhole).
# Addresses in house_direct_ip.allow still pass. off lets them through.
#HOUSE_BLOCK_DIRECT_IP=on
# Plain HTTP: on rejects all house connections to TCP 80, by name or
# by address. It can break captive portals, some TVs and printers,
# the Android "no internet" check and old apt mirrors. Off by default.
#HOUSE_BLOCK_HTTP=off
# Own VPNs: on drops the own VPN of a house device. Thus the device cannot
# send its traffic and DNS around the Pi: WireGuard on any port (by its header),
# OpenVPN on 1194, and the VPN/DoH/proxy domain feed in the house
# resolver. It does not affect IPsec (Wi-Fi calling). It also stops Tailscale
# and Cloudflare WARP. off lets them all through.
#HOUSE_BLOCK_VPN=on
# Ports through which the house may go out. strict (default): web (80, and
# 443 and the other TLS ports 465 993 5223 5228 8443; each new flow is checked
# by the name that it sends), NTP and ping, plus the toggles below. All other
# traffic is dropped and logged house-port. audit: the same rules log
# house-audit and pass, so that you see first what strict would break. open:
# all ports. Local addresses (also the page of the uplink router) are
# dropped in all modes.
#HOUSE_EGRESS=strict
# Wi-Fi calling: IPsec (UDP 500/4500, ESP) to all addresses. When on, it
# also lets an IKEv2 VPN through.
#HOUSE_ALLOW_WIFI_CALLING=off
# UDP of call apps (Meet, Zoom, Teams, WhatsApp, FaceTime). When off, they
# relay over TCP 443: calls work, with a little more delay.
#HOUSE_ALLOW_CALL_UDP=off
# WhatsApp: its chat protocol is not TLS, so the name check cannot read
# it. on lets TCP 5222, 80 and non-TLS 443 go to the Meta ranges
# (policy/house_whatsapp.ips) and to no other place. TLS to Meta is still
# checked by name. off: WhatsApp messages stop on the house.
#HOUSE_ALLOW_WHATSAPP=on
# Extra ports, for example for a game: "tcp:27015-27030 udp:3074". The
# name check does not apply to a TLS port that is named here.
#HOUSE_ALLOW_PORTS=
# WireGuard egress for the house segment (WG_IF in
# docs/user_guide/home_network.md). Empty:
# no tunnel. The house goes out through WAN_IF as before. Put the Mullvad
# Linux config at /etc/pi-fortress/mullvad.conf (root 0600). apply rewrites
# /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf from it (Table=off, v4 only, no DNS=).
#WG_IF=wg0
# fwmark for destinations that bypass the tunnel (banks, UPI). 2b fills
# vpn_bypass_v4. 2a renders the empty set and the mark rule.
#WG_BYPASS_MARK=0x1
